# API Reporter Security Model – End-to-End Proposal (mTLS with Technical User)

## Objective

Secure the **API Reporter** endpoint so that only the authorised consumer robot can access it using a **TLS client certificate** associated with the technical user **t910212**.

The goal is to achieve this **without modifying the Python/FastAPI application code**.

---

# End-to-End Flow

```text
                    +--------------------------------------+
                    | Consumer Robot                      |
                    | Technical User: t910212            |
                    |                                    |
                    | Client Certificate (t910212-cert)  |
                    | Private Key (t910212-key)          |
                    +------------------+-----------------+
                                       |
                                       | HTTPS + Mutual TLS
                                       |
                                       v
                    +--------------------------------------+
                    | Apache HTTPD on RCM Server          |
                    |                                    |
                    | Validate client certificate         |
                    | using ssl/cacerts.pem              |
                    |                                    |
                    | Authorise only CN=t910212          |
                    +------------------+-----------------+
                                       |
                                       | Local Proxy
                                       |
                                       v
                    +--------------------------------------+
                    | FastAPI API Reporter                |
                    | GET /reporter/api/reporter          |
                    |                                    |
                    | Reads Oracle View                  |
                    | Returns JSON                       |
                    +------------------+-----------------+
                                       |
                                       v
                                 Oracle 19c
```

---

# Responsibilities

## Consumer Robot Server

### Install

The consumer robot must receive:

- `t910212-cert.pem`
- `t910212-key.pem`

These are the certificate and private key associated with the technical user **t910212**.

The private key **must remain only on the consumer robot**.

### Configure the Robot

The robot must invoke

```
https://fcscmt-actone-uat-ch.appl.ubs.net/reporter/api/reporter
```

presenting

- the client certificate
- the corresponding private key

during the TLS handshake.

No username/password authentication is required.

---

## RCM Server (Apache HTTPD)

### Existing CA

The existing file

```
ssl/cacerts.pem
```

contains the trusted UBS CA certificates.

This file is used only to verify the certificate presented by the consumer robot.

### No change to cacerts.pem

The certificate

```
t910212-cert.pem
```

**must NOT be imported into**

```
ssl/cacerts.pem
```

The CA bundle must continue to contain only trusted CA certificates.

---

## Apache Configuration

Protect only the Reporter endpoint by requiring a client certificate.

Example:

```apache
<Location /reporter/>

    SSLVerifyClient require
    SSLVerifyDepth 5

    <RequireAll>
        Require ssl-verify-client
        Require expr "%{SSL_CLIENT_S_DN_CN} == 't910212'"
    </RequireAll>

</Location>
```

This ensures that:

- only a valid client certificate is accepted;
- the certificate must be issued by the trusted CA;
- the certificate identity must correspond to **t910212**.

---

# Python API Reporter

No code modification is required.

The application continues to expose:

```
GET /reporter/api/reporter
```

and simply returns the Oracle data.

Authentication is completely handled by Apache before the request reaches FastAPI.

---

# Certificate Validation Process

```text
Consumer Robot
      |
      | presents
      |
      +--> t910212-cert.pem
      +--> proves ownership of t910212-key.pem
                    |
                    v
Apache HTTPD
      |
      | validates certificate
      | against
      |
      +--> ssl/cacerts.pem
      |
      | checks CN = t910212
      |
      +--> Request accepted
```

---

# Summary

## Consumer Robot

- Install `t910212-cert.pem`
- Install `t910212-key.pem`
- Configure the HTTP client to present the certificate during the HTTPS connection
- Continue calling the existing Reporter URL

---

## RCM Server

- Keep the existing `ssl/cacerts.pem`
- **Do not import the technical user certificate into the CA bundle**
- Protect `/reporter/` using `SSLVerifyClient`
- Authorise only the certificate belonging to technical user **t910212**

---

## Python API Reporter

- No code changes
- No authentication logic added
- No certificate management inside the application

---

# Benefits

- No changes to the FastAPI application.
- Authentication is centralized in Apache HTTPD.
- The private key never leaves the consumer robot.
- The RCM server trusts only certificates issued by the internal UBS CA.
- Access to the Reporter endpoint is restricted to the authorised technical user (`t910212`).
